## Extension questions
1. **Book "any DOUBLE room" instead of a specific one:** iterate free rooms and attempt `book` until one succeeds (another thread may win first).
2. **Inventory-count model:** large OTAs track counts per room type per date (`Map<date, available>`) rather than individual rooms; a booking decrements each night atomically and the hotel assigns room numbers at check-in.
3. **Distributed:** DB table `room_night(room_id, date)` with a unique constraint, or optimistic locking on per-date inventory rows.
4. **Invoice with extras:** `Invoice` aggregating room charges and services (Decorator or line items), taxes via strategy.
5. **Holds during payment:** temporary hold with expiry, similar to BookMyShow seat locks.

## Problem
Design an in-memory publish-subscribe message queue (a common Flipkart/PhonePe machine-coding question). Publishers send messages to named topics; subscribers register on topics and consume messages independently and concurrently, each at its own pace.

## Requirements
**P0**
1. Create topics; publish messages to a topic.
2. Multiple subscribers per topic; every subscriber receives every message of the topic (fan-out).
3. Subscribers consume in parallel and in order; a slow subscriber must not block others or the publisher.
4. Each subscriber tracks its own **offset**; it can be reset to replay messages.
5. Thread-safe.

**P1:** consumer groups (each message to one member of a group), retries/dead-letter queue, message TTL/retention, partitions, back-pressure.

## Entities
`Message`, `Topic` (append-only list of messages), `Subscriber` (interface with `consume`), `TopicSubscriber` (subscriber + offset), `SubscriberWorker` (thread per subscription), `TopicHandler`, `Broker` (facade API).

## Class diagram
```text
Broker (facade)
  - topics: ConcurrentHashMap<name, Topic>
  - handlers: ConcurrentHashMap<name, TopicHandler>
  + createTopic(name), subscribe(topic, subscriber), publish(topic, msg), resetOffset(topic, sub, offset)

Topic          - name, messages: CopyOnWriteArrayList<Message>  (append-only log)
TopicSubscriber- subscriber, offset: AtomicInteger
TopicHandler   - topic, workers: Map<subscriberId, SubscriberWorker>
               + publish(): wakes all workers
SubscriberWorker implements Runnable
  loop: while offset < topic.size -> consume(messages[offset]), offset++
        else wait() until notified

<<interface>> Subscriber  + id(), consume(Message)
```

## Design choices (Kafka-like)
- Messages are **appended to the topic log and never removed** on consumption; each subscriber has its own offset. This gives fan-out, replay, and independent speeds for free.
- Each subscription has a **dedicated worker thread** that sleeps (`wait`) when caught up and is woken (`notify`) on publish. In production you would use a thread pool and push to per-subscriber queues; the offset model stays.
- `publish` is O(1) and never blocks on consumers.

## Patterns used and why
- **Observer / Publish-Subscribe**: topics notify registered subscribers; publishers and subscribers are fully decoupled.
- **Facade**: `Broker` provides a tiny API over topics, handlers and workers.
- **Producer-consumer** with guarded wait/notify per subscriber worker.
- **Strategy (extension)**: retry policy, delivery semantics (at-most-once vs at-least-once).

## Java implementation
```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.*;

record Message(String id, String payload, long timestamp) { }

interface Subscriber {
    String id();
    void consume(Message m) throws Exception;
}

class Topic {
    private final String name;
    private final List<Message> messages = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
    Topic(String name) { this.name = name; }
    String name() { return name; }
    void append(Message m) { messages.add(m); }
    int size() { return messages.size(); }
    Message get(int i) { return messages.get(i); }
}

class TopicSubscriber {
    final Subscriber subscriber;
    final AtomicInteger offset = new AtomicInteger(0);
    TopicSubscriber(Subscriber s) { subscriber = s; }
}

class SubscriberWorker implements Runnable {
    private final Topic topic;
    private final TopicSubscriber ts;
    private volatile boolean running = true;

    SubscriberWorker(Topic topic, TopicSubscriber ts) { this.topic = topic; this.ts = ts; }

    public void run() {
        try {
            while (running) {
                Message m; int idx;
                synchronized (ts) {
                    while (running && ts.offset.get() >= topic.size()) ts.wait();   // guarded wait
                    if (!running) break;
                    idx = ts.offset.get();
                    m = topic.get(idx);
                }
                try {
                    ts.subscriber.consume(m);
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    System.out.println("  " + ts.subscriber.id() + " failed on " + m.id() + ": " + e.getMessage() + " (skipping)");
                }
                ts.offset.compareAndSet(idx, idx + 1);     // no-op if offset was reset meanwhile
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) { Thread.currentThread().interrupt(); }
    }

    void wake() { synchronized (ts) { ts.notify(); } }
    void stop() { running = false; wake(); }
}

class TopicHandler {
    private final Topic topic;
    private final Map<String, SubscriberWorker> workers = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final Map<String, TopicSubscriber> subs = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    TopicHandler(Topic topic) { this.topic = topic; }

    void addSubscriber(Subscriber s) {
        TopicSubscriber ts = new TopicSubscriber(s);
        SubscriberWorker w = new SubscriberWorker(topic, ts);
        if (subs.putIfAbsent(s.id(), ts) != null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Already subscribed: " + s.id());
        workers.put(s.id(), w);
        Thread t = new Thread(w, "worker-" + topic.name() + "-" + s.id());
        t.setDaemon(true);
        t.start();
    }

    void publish() { workers.values().forEach(SubscriberWorker::wake); }

    void resetOffset(String subId, int offset) {
        TopicSubscriber ts = subs.get(subId);
        synchronized (ts) { ts.offset.set(offset); }
        workers.get(subId).wake();
    }

    void shutdown() { workers.values().forEach(SubscriberWorker::stop); }
}
```

```java
class Broker {
    private final Map<String, Topic> topics = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final Map<String, TopicHandler> handlers = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final AtomicLong ids = new AtomicLong();

    void createTopic(String name) {
        Topic t = new Topic(name);
        if (topics.putIfAbsent(name, t) != null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Topic exists: " + name);
        handlers.put(name, new TopicHandler(t));
    }

    void subscribe(String topic, Subscriber s) { handler(topic).addSubscriber(s); }

    String publish(String topic, String payload) {
        Topic t = topics.get(topic);
        if (t == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("No topic " + topic);
        Message m = new Message("M" + ids.incrementAndGet(), payload, System.currentTimeMillis());
        t.append(m);
        handler(topic).publish();
        return m.id();
    }

    void resetOffset(String topic, String subId, int offset) { handler(topic).resetOffset(subId, offset); }
    void shutdown() { handlers.values().forEach(TopicHandler::shutdown); }

    private TopicHandler handler(String topic) {
        TopicHandler h = handlers.get(topic);
        if (h == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("No topic " + topic);
        return h;
    }
}

class PrintingSubscriber implements Subscriber {
    private final String id; private final long delayMs;
    final List<String> received = Collections.synchronizedList(new ArrayList<>());
    PrintingSubscriber(String id, long delayMs) { this.id = id; this.delayMs = delayMs; }
    public String id() { return id; }
    public void consume(Message m) throws Exception {
        Thread.sleep(delayMs);                         // simulate work; slow consumer
        if (m.payload().contains("bad")) throw new IllegalArgumentException("cannot parse");
        received.add(m.payload());
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Broker broker = new Broker();
        broker.createTopic("orders");
        PrintingSubscriber fast = new PrintingSubscriber("analytics", 5);
        PrintingSubscriber slow = new PrintingSubscriber("email", 40);
        broker.subscribe("orders", fast);
        broker.subscribe("orders", slow);

        long t0 = System.currentTimeMillis();
        for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++) broker.publish("orders", "order-" + i);
        broker.publish("orders", "bad-order");
        System.out.println("Publisher finished in " + (System.currentTimeMillis() - t0) + " ms (not blocked by slow consumer)");

        Thread.sleep(400);
        System.out.println("analytics got " + fast.received);
        System.out.println("email got     " + slow.received);

        broker.resetOffset("orders", "analytics", 2);   // replay from offset 2
        Thread.sleep(200);
        System.out.println("analytics after replay " + fast.received);
        try { broker.publish("payments", "x"); } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) { System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage()); }
        broker.shutdown();
    }
}
```

## Extension questions
1. **Consumer groups:** subscribers in the same group share one offset (or partitions are assigned to members), so each message goes to one member - competing consumers.
2. **At-least-once delivery and retries:** advance the offset only after successful `consume`; retry with backoff N times, then publish to a dead-letter topic.
3. **Retention:** drop messages older than T or beyond N per topic; offsets become absolute (store base offset).
4. **Partitions for scale:** a topic split into partitions by key hash preserves per-key ordering while allowing parallel consumers.
5. **Thread pool instead of thread per subscriber:** each publish schedules a drain task per subscriber on an executor; an `AtomicBoolean` "draining" flag per subscriber keeps ordering.
6. **Back-pressure:** bounded topics where publish blocks or fails when consumers lag too far.

## Problem
Design the backend core of an e-commerce platform: sellers add products and stock per warehouse; customers add items to a cart and place orders; inventory must never oversell; orders move through a lifecycle; stakeholders get notified.

## Requirements
**P0**
1. Product catalogue (id, name, price) and stock per warehouse.
2. Cart: add/remove items, compute total.
3. Place order: **reserve** stock atomically for all items (all-or-nothing), then pay; on success **commit** (deduct), on failure **release**.
4. Order lifecycle: `CREATED -> PAID -> SHIPPED -> DELIVERED`, cancellation allowed before shipping (stock returned).
5. Notify customer on status changes; alert when stock drops below a threshold.
6. Concurrent orders for the last unit: exactly one succeeds.

**P1:** multiple warehouses with nearest-warehouse selection, coupons, returns/refunds, partial shipments.

## Entities
`Product`, `InventoryItem` (available + reserved), `Warehouse`, `InventoryService`, `Cart`, `CartItem`, `Order`, `OrderItem`, `OrderStatus`, `PaymentGateway`, `OrderService`, `OrderObserver`.

## Class diagram
```text
Product      - id, name, price (paise)
InventoryItem- productId, available, reserved, lowStockThreshold
               + reserve(q), release(q), commit(q)    (synchronized)
InventoryService
  - items: ConcurrentHashMap<productId, InventoryItem>
  + reserveAll(Map<productId, qty>): boolean   (all-or-nothing, ordered locking)
  + releaseAll(...), commitAll(...)

Cart - userId, items: Map<productId, qty>   + add, remove, total(catalog)
Order - id, userId, items: List<OrderItem>, amount, status: OrderStatus
        + transitionTo(next)  (validated by OrderStatus.canMoveTo)

<<interface>> PaymentGateway   + pay(orderId, amount): boolean   ^.. FakeGateway
<<interface>> OrderObserver    + onStatusChange(order, old, new)  ^.. CustomerNotifier, ^.. AnalyticsObserver
<<interface>> StockObserver    + onLowStock(productId, available)

OrderService (facade)
  + placeOrder(cart): Order
  + ship(orderId), deliver(orderId), cancel(orderId)
```

## Key design decisions
- **Reserve-then-commit** (two-phase) prevents overselling while payment is in progress, and lets failures roll back cleanly.
- **All-or-nothing across items:** lock inventory items in a **consistent order (sorted product id)** to avoid deadlocks when two carts contain the same products in different orders; roll back partial reservations on failure.
- **Order status as an enum with allowed transitions** - a lightweight State pattern; illegal transitions throw.
- **Observers** decouple notifications/analytics/low-stock alerts from core logic.
- **Money in paise** (long) to avoid floating point errors.

## Java implementation
```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.*;

record Product(String id, String name, long price) { }

class InventoryItem {
    final String productId; private int available, reserved; final int lowStockThreshold;
    InventoryItem(String productId, int available, int threshold) { this.productId = productId; this.available = available; this.lowStockThreshold = threshold; }
    boolean tryReserve(int q) { if (available < q) return false; available -= q; reserved += q; return true; }
    void release(int q) { reserved -= q; available += q; }
    void commit(int q) { reserved -= q; }
    void restock(int q) { available += q; }
    int available() { return available; }
}

interface StockObserver { void onLowStock(String productId, int available); }

class InventoryService {
    private final Map<String, InventoryItem> items = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final List<StockObserver> observers = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();

    void addStock(String productId, int qty, int threshold) {
        items.computeIfAbsent(productId, k -> new InventoryItem(k, 0, threshold));
        InventoryItem it = items.get(productId);
        synchronized (it) { it.restock(qty); }
    }
    void addObserver(StockObserver o) { observers.add(o); }
    int available(String pid) { InventoryItem it = items.get(pid); synchronized (it) { return it.available(); } }

    /** All-or-nothing reservation. Locks items in sorted order to avoid deadlock. */
    boolean reserveAll(Map<String, Integer> req) {
        List<String> ids = new ArrayList<>(new TreeSet<>(req.keySet()));
        return reserveRec(ids, 0, req);
    }
    private boolean reserveRec(List<String> ids, int i, Map<String, Integer> req) {
        if (i == ids.size()) return true;
        InventoryItem it = items.get(ids.get(i));
        if (it == null) return false;
        synchronized (it) {                             // nested locks, acquired in sorted order
            if (!it.tryReserve(req.get(it.productId))) return false;
            if (reserveRec(ids, i + 1, req)) return true;
            it.release(req.get(it.productId));          // roll back this one if later items failed
            return false;
        }
    }
    void releaseAll(Map<String, Integer> req) {
        req.forEach((pid, q) -> { InventoryItem it = items.get(pid); synchronized (it) { it.release(q); } });
    }
    void commitAll(Map<String, Integer> req) {
        req.forEach((pid, q) -> {
            InventoryItem it = items.get(pid);
            int left;
            synchronized (it) { it.commit(q); left = it.available(); }
            if (left <= it.lowStockThreshold) observers.forEach(o -> o.onLowStock(pid, left));
        });
    }
}

class Cart {
    final String userId; final Map<String, Integer> items = new LinkedHashMap<>();
    Cart(String userId) { this.userId = userId; }
    Cart add(String pid, int q) { if (q <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("qty > 0"); items.merge(pid, q, Integer::sum); return this; }
    void remove(String pid) { items.remove(pid); }
}

enum OrderStatus {
    CREATED, PAID, SHIPPED, DELIVERED, CANCELLED, PAYMENT_FAILED;
    boolean canMoveTo(OrderStatus next) {
        return switch (this) {
            case CREATED -> next == PAID || next == PAYMENT_FAILED || next == CANCELLED;
            case PAID -> next == SHIPPED || next == CANCELLED;
            case SHIPPED -> next == DELIVERED;
            default -> false;                            // terminal states
        };
    }
}

record OrderItem(String productId, int qty, long unitPrice) { }

class Order {
    final String id, userId; final List<OrderItem> items; final long amount;
    private OrderStatus status = OrderStatus.CREATED;
    Order(String id, String userId, List<OrderItem> items) {
        this.id = id; this.userId = userId; this.items = List.copyOf(items);
        this.amount = items.stream().mapToLong(i -> i.qty() * i.unitPrice()).sum();
    }
    OrderStatus status() { return status; }
    synchronized OrderStatus transitionTo(OrderStatus next) {
        if (!status.canMoveTo(next)) throw new IllegalStateException("Order " + id + ": " + status + " -> " + next + " not allowed");
        OrderStatus old = status; status = next; return old;
    }
    Map<String, Integer> quantities() {
        Map<String, Integer> m = new HashMap<>();
        items.forEach(i -> m.merge(i.productId(), i.qty(), Integer::sum));
        return m;
    }
}
```

```java
interface PaymentGateway { boolean pay(String orderId, long amount); }
interface OrderObserver { void onStatusChange(Order o, OrderStatus from, OrderStatus to); }

class OutOfStockException extends RuntimeException { OutOfStockException(String m) { super(m); } }

class OrderService {
    private final Map<String, Product> catalog;
    private final InventoryService inventory;
    private final PaymentGateway payments;
    private final List<OrderObserver> observers = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
    private final Map<String, Order> orders = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final AtomicLong seq = new AtomicLong();

    OrderService(Map<String, Product> catalog, InventoryService inv, PaymentGateway pg) { this.catalog = catalog; inventory = inv; payments = pg; }
    void addObserver(OrderObserver o) { observers.add(o); }

    Order placeOrder(Cart cart) {
        if (cart.items.isEmpty()) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Cart is empty");
        List<OrderItem> items = new ArrayList<>();
        cart.items.forEach((pid, q) -> items.add(new OrderItem(pid, q, catalog.get(pid).price())));
        Order order = new Order("O" + seq.incrementAndGet(), cart.userId, items);
        Map<String, Integer> qty = order.quantities();

        if (!inventory.reserveAll(qty)) throw new OutOfStockException("Insufficient stock for order of " + cart.userId);
        orders.put(order.id, order);
        if (payments.pay(order.id, order.amount)) {
            inventory.commitAll(qty);
            move(order, OrderStatus.PAID);
        } else {
            inventory.releaseAll(qty);
            move(order, OrderStatus.PAYMENT_FAILED);
        }
        cart.items.clear();
        return order;
    }

    void ship(String id) { move(get(id), OrderStatus.SHIPPED); }
    void deliver(String id) { move(get(id), OrderStatus.DELIVERED); }

    void cancel(String id) {
        Order o = get(id);
        move(o, OrderStatus.CANCELLED);
        o.quantities().forEach((pid, q) -> inventory.addStock(pid, q, 0));   // return stock (and refund in real life)
    }

    private void move(Order o, OrderStatus to) {
        OrderStatus from = o.transitionTo(to);
        observers.forEach(obs -> obs.onStatusChange(o, from, to));
    }
    private Order get(String id) {
        Order o = orders.get(id);
        if (o == null) throw new IllegalArgumentException("No order " + id);
        return o;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Map<String, Product> catalog = Map.of(
            "P1", new Product("P1", "iPhone", 7_999_900),
            "P2", new Product("P2", "Case", 49_900));
        InventoryService inv = new InventoryService();
        inv.addStock("P1", 1, 0);
        inv.addStock("P2", 10, 3);
        inv.addObserver((pid, left) -> System.out.println("  [ALERT] low stock " + pid + " left=" + left));

        PaymentGateway pg = (orderId, amount) -> !orderId.equals("O99");   // fake: everything succeeds except O99
        OrderService svc = new OrderService(catalog, inv, pg);
        svc.addObserver((o, from, to) -> System.out.println("  [notify " + o.userId + "] " + o.id + " " + from + " -> " + to));

        // Two users race for the single iPhone
        ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);
        List<Future<String>> res = new ArrayList<>();
        for (String user : List.of("raj", "anu")) {
            res.add(pool.submit(() -> {
                try { return user + ": " + svc.placeOrder(new Cart(user).add("P1", 1).add("P2", 2)).id; }
                catch (OutOfStockException e) { return user + ": " + e.getMessage(); }
            }));
        }
        for (Future<String> f : res) System.out.println(f.get());
        pool.shutdown();
        System.out.println("iPhone left=" + inv.available("P1") + ", cases left=" + inv.available("P2"));

        Order o2 = svc.placeOrder(new Cart("meera").add("P2", 5));
        svc.ship(o2.id);
        try { svc.cancel(o2.id); } catch (IllegalStateException e) { System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage()); }
        svc.deliver(o2.id);
        Order o3 = svc.placeOrder(new Cart("dev").add("P2", 1));
        svc.cancel(o3.id);
        System.out.println("cases left after cancel=" + inv.available("P2"));
    }
}
